\f4\fs26 The song continued to be belted out when the funeral procession parted, from the northern to the southern end of the stadium and a small group of 6 Elvi, carrying a coffin, entered the stadium. Spotlights burst into life and stung the coffin detail with beams of pure white as they made their way slowly and rhythmically to the centre of the ground where the coffin was placed high atop a massive pile of combustible material comprising mostly of rubbish collected during the stadium clean-up, but also some serious lumps of wood they had stumbled across. The funeral parade became silent and then, in a much practiced spiral pattern, the entire funeral parade began passing by the pyre and throwing their torches on top and then fading back into the crowd. \
The spotlights faded as the flames reached higher, lighting up the entire stadium with orange sobbing faces and as it died down one acoustic guitar, at the far end of the stadium, was heard strumming lightly. Then another, just near to the private box, replied to the lonely instrument, which return serve as another guitar was strummed, then another and another until 65,000 acoustic guitars were playing in unison. Voices from the field below chimed in and then every light in the stadium flashed brightly before fading to nothing. Neon lights, lasers and strobes all joined into the deafening cacophony of 65,000 guitars and 100,000 voices all slipping seamlessly from song to song. The black clad Elvi in the parade, in time to the music and in unison with each other, removed their outer garments to reveal highly colourful and glittering outfits that reflected both light and joy. The continuum song ended abruptly in perfect synchronicity and the entire crowd jumped to their feet. It was was over all too quickly, only 90 minutes, but the wake was planned to run over several days. The entire stadium then broke out into wild applause and cheering. The partying and dancing began.\
\'93That was truly amazing! Wow, I am glad I was patching for that!\'94 Dr Logan looked like a smile on legs. \'93That was an unprecedented cultural event. Thank you for inviting me, Cracker, thank you.\'94\
\'93In the quarter I am the Great Teacher, Holy Aunt Kathy.\'94 He joked. \'93These guys take it all seriously, even if I can\'92t.\'94\
\'93Where are Hayley and Sarah?\'94 Kathy asked, shooting glances in all directions. \'93Okay, I see them. It looks like they are having a deep and meaningful.\'94\
 \
\'93Lets get down to the field and join in. Got patches?\'94 Cracker was ready to let his hair down, again. \

